WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.140
In winter, a bare tree looks dead.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.820
It's easy to walk past the same tree and miss its slow changes.

3
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.000
Yet one tree, visited through the year, tells a very different story.

4
00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.613
Adopting one tree slows the year down.

5
00:00:18.873 --> 00:00:23.513
Your child practices looking closely and recording slow changes over time.

6
00:00:24.653 --> 00:00:27.973
They make a guess, wait, and check it against real evidence.

7
00:00:29.173 --> 00:00:31.953
In thirty minutes to start, you set up a whole year.

8
00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:35.543
Choose a tree that drops its leaves in fall.

9
00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:38.023
Ask permission to visit.

10
00:00:39.323 --> 00:00:41.923
Bring a phone or camera, paper, and a pencil.

11
00:00:43.423 --> 00:00:45.763
Stand ten to twenty steps back by a landmark.

12
00:00:47.043 --> 00:00:50.583
Take every photo from that same spot, facing the same way.

13
00:00:51.823 --> 00:00:53.263
Keep the whole tree in the frame.

14
00:00:54.317 --> 00:00:57.677
Before looking closely, let your child predict first.

15
00:00:58.997 --> 00:01:01.657
Ask, 'What do you think this tree will look like next month?'

16
00:01:02.257 --> 00:01:07.637
Save the guess. Spend about ten minutes looking at bark, a low twig, the weather,

17
00:01:07.877 --> 00:01:09.117
and any animals nearby.

18
00:01:10.557 --> 00:01:13.677
Your child draws one twig or leaf to save in a folder.

19
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:18.860
Come back about once a month for fifteen minutes, or once each season.

20
00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:21.560
Repeat the photo and drawing.

21
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:23.940
Record what you saw.

22
00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.240
Check the last guess, then compare photos.

23
00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.360
Ask, 'Can you find three differences?'

24
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:33.373
Now picture your winter visit.

25
00:01:34.613 --> 00:01:37.533
The branches are bare, and your child says, 'Our tree died.'

26
00:01:38.153 --> 00:01:40.153
Before you explain, pause for a moment.

27
00:01:41.293 --> 00:01:45.193
What do you predict you'll see if you look closely at a bare winter twig?

28
00:01:50.683 --> 00:01:52.783
Look closely at a bare twig.

29
00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:56.363
Plump buds wait at the tip and where each leaf joined.

30
00:01:57.763 --> 00:01:59.803
Ask, 'I wonder what is inside this bud.

31
00:02:00.923 --> 00:02:02.123
What do you think will come out?'

32
00:02:02.603 --> 00:02:07.503
The tree is dormant, alive but resting, with next spring's leaves folded inside.

33
00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:13.807
Shorter days and cooler weather in fall signal the tree to drop its leaves before

34
00:02:13.807 --> 00:02:17.427
winter. Warmer spring days wake those buds.

35
00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:23.027
When you finish all four seasons, put one picture from each season in order.

36
00:02:24.307 --> 00:02:27.067
Look at the order together and ask what comes next.

37
00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:30.347
Stay with your child on every visit.

38
00:02:31.687 --> 00:02:34.767
Avoid busy road crossings, storms, and strong wind.

39
00:02:36.087 --> 00:02:38.127
Feet stay on the ground, with no climbing.

40
00:02:39.407 --> 00:02:44.767
Nothing goes in a mouth, and small acorns, nuts, or stones can choke children under

41
00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.827
four. Call nine one one if choking.

42
00:02:49.017 --> 00:02:51.157
Check the trunk for poison ivy.

43
00:02:52.217 --> 00:02:55.557
Leave fallen nuts alone, especially with a nut allergy.

44
00:02:56.877 --> 00:02:59.677
Never taste wild plants, berries, or mushrooms.

45
00:03:01.037 --> 00:03:02.857
Look at insects without touching them.

46
00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:05.677
Adults handle glass lenses.

47
00:03:06.977 --> 00:03:08.857
Keep lenses from focusing sunlight.

48
00:03:10.137 --> 00:03:11.737
Never look at the sun through one.

49
00:03:12.917 --> 00:03:14.397
Wash hands and check for ticks.

50
00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:19.670
By year's end, one ordinary tree becomes your child's calendar.

51
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:24.910
Next winter, look for buds together when the branches turn bare again.

52
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.550
Those tiny buds mean spring is already waiting.
